            ":step/content": {
              ":db/id": 17592186056040,
              ":tutorial/content": "We can use subscripts and superscripts to limit the special sets to being only positive (\"$+$\" superscript), only negative (\"$-$\" superscript), and to include zero (\"$0$\" subscript).\n\nFor example, $\\mathbb{Z}^+$ represents the positive integers, while $\\mathbb{Z}^-$ represents the negative integers:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Z}^{+} & =\\{1,2,3,\u2026\\} \\\\ {Z}^{-} & =\\{-1,-2,-3,\u2026\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThese sets do not include $0.$ If we want to include $0$ too, then we can use a subscript $0,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Z}_{0}^{+} & =\\{0,1,2,3,\u2026\\} \\\\ {Z}_{0}^{-} & =\\{0,-1,-2,-3,\u2026\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nA table describing all the special sets is given below.\n\n| Symbol | Meaning |\n| --- | --- |\n| $\\emptyset$ | The empty set, $\\{\\}$ |\n| $\\mathbb{N}$ | The set of natural numbers, $\\{1,2,3,...\\}$ |\n| $\\mathbb{N}_0$ | The set of natural numbers and zero,  $\\{0,1,2,3,...\\}$ |\n| $\\mathbb{Z}$ | The set of integers, $\\{0,\\pm1,\\pm2,\\pm3,...\\}$ |\n| $\\mathbb{Z}^+$ | The set of positive integers, $\\{1,2,3,...\\}.$ |\n| $\\mathbb{Z}_0^+$ | The set of positive integers and zero, $\\{0,1,2,3,...\\}$ |\n| $\\mathbb{Z}^-$ | The set of negative integers, $\\{-1,-2,-3,...\\}$ |\n| $\\mathbb{Z}_0^-$ | The set of negative integers and zero, $\\{0,-1,-2,-3,...\\}$ |\n| $\\mathbb{Q}$ | The set of rational numbers |\n| $\\mathbb{Q}^+$ | The set of positive rational numbers |\n| $\\mathbb{Q}_0^+$ | The set of positive rational numbers and zero |\n| $\\mathbb{Q}^-$ | The set of negative rational numbers |\n| $\\mathbb{Q}_0^-$ | The set of negative rational numbers and zero |\n| $\\mathbb{R}$ | The set of real numbers |\n| $\\mathbb{R}^+$ | The set of positive real numbers |\n| $\\mathbb{R}_0^+$ | The set of positive real numbers and zero |\n| $\\mathbb{R}^-$ | The set of negative real numbers |\n| $\\mathbb{R}_0^-$ | The set of negative real numbers and zero |",
              ":tutorial/id": "05d0929b-b494-531b-9eea-35af04606555",
              ":tutorial/math-academy-id": 8215,
              ":tutorial/title": "Subscript and Superscript Notation With Special Sets"
            },
